<task id="002" project="spaarkeai-compose-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>`SpeFileStore` version-content fetch (FR-06) — fetch a driveItem version's content by `versionId`</title>
    <phase>0 Foundations</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W0</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,spe,azure,graph</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
    <assigned>unassigned</assigned>
    <started></started>
    <completed></completed>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Extend the SPE facade (`ISpeFileOperations` / `SpeFileStore`) with a method that fetches a specific
    driveItem **version's** content by `versionId` — Graph route `/drives/{driveId}/items/{itemId}/versions/{versionId}/content`.
    This is the FR-06 baseline-retrieval capability: E1's delta save applies edits onto the **load-time**
    SPE version (captured by `versionId` at Load), which stays addressable even after prior dirty saves
    have advanced the file's current version (design §4.3, S4). The method MUST live behind the facade —
    NO `Microsoft.Graph` types (`GraphServiceClient`, `DriveItem`, `DriveItemVersion`) may leak above
    `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure (ADR-007). This is an additive facade method that mirrors the existing
    `DownloadFileAsUserAsync` OBO shape; it adds no consumer wiring (task 022 consumes it).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer fluent in the Microsoft Graph SDK v5 (driveItem versions endpoint), the
    OBO (on-behalf-of) auth flow used by the Spaarke SPE facade, and the `SpeFileStore` /
    `ISpeFileOperations` boundary discipline (ADR-007 — all Graph access stays behind the facade, only
    byte streams / DTOs cross the boundary). Comfortable adding a version-scoped content download that
    mirrors the existing item-content download.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `ISpeFileOperations` gains a version-content fetch (e.g. `DownloadFileVersionAsUserAsync(HttpContext,
    driveId, itemId, versionId, ct)` returning `Task&lt;Stream?&gt;`), implemented in `SpeFileStore` via the
    Graph `/versions/{versionId}/content` route under the caller's OBO token. No `Microsoft.Graph` type
    appears in the public signature or above the facade. Matching unit tests in
    `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/…` mock at the facade/Graph boundary (ADR-038 — no
    `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`) and cover the happy path (correct version bytes returned) plus the
    not-found / missing-version negative. BFF build green; the method is additive (existing callers/mocks
    untouched).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      E1's baseline (design §4.3, Spike S4 decision) is the **load-time SPE version fetched by
      `versionId`**, captured at Load. SPE versions files, so the load-time original stays addressable
      after later dirty saves degrade the *current* version — this is authoritative, refresh-safe, and
      needs zero new storage. The one missing capability is a `SpeFileStore` method to fetch a *specific*
      version's content (the current facade only downloads the item's current content via
      `DownloadFileAsUserAsync`, `ISpeFileOperations.cs:42`). The Graph route `/versions/{id}/content` is
      a known capability (spec Unresolved Question — "validate the Graph route early"). This task lands
      that additive method so the E1 cutover (task 022) can retrieve the correct baseline; the client
      `state.docxBytes` remains a same-session fast-path and a size-capped Redis cache is the fallback.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/ISpeFileOperations.cs — add the version-content fetch to the facade contract (mirror `DownloadFileAsUserAsync`, line 42); all SPE access stays behind it (ADR-007)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — implement the version-content fetch via Graph `/drives/{driveId}/items/{itemId}/versions/{versionId}/content` under OBO; reuse the existing download OBO pattern, do NOT reimplement auth</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — existing `DownloadFileAsUserAsync` implementation (OBO token acquisition + Graph call shape to mirror)</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/notes/spikes/S1b-S2-S4-S5-2026-07-16.md — S4 baseline-source decision (load-time version by `versionId`)</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §4.3 (where the baseline lives — S4), §9 (BFF surface), §10 (SPE facade reuse row)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="n/a">No task dependency (parallel-safe with task 001 — different files). Consumed by task 022 (E1 cutover baseline retrieval).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">NO `Microsoft.Graph` types above the `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure facade. The new method's public signature exposes only primitives + `HttpContext` + `Stream?`; `GraphServiceClient`, `DriveItem`, `DriveItemVersion`, and other `Microsoft.Graph` types stay inside `SpeFileStore.cs`. No Graph type leaks into `Services/Compose/` or endpoints.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Version-content fetch is invoked under the caller's OBO identity (same as `DownloadFileAsUserAsync`); authorization is enforced at the consuming endpoint, not via new global middleware.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-005 / ADR-009 / ADR-015">The version bytes are Tier-3-isolated document content; any future baseline cache is Redis-first (ADR-009) — but this task adds only the fetch, not a cache.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-038">Matching tests mock at the facade/Graph boundary — NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests. The consuming through-the-wire seam test rides task 022/024; this task's unit tests assert the version route + return-shape + not-found negative.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 / §10">No new NuGet package (Graph SDK already referenced) → ~0 MB publish delta; still report absolute + delta vs the ~49.63 MB baseline per the per-task rule. State the PDB convention.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification for the additive facade method in the PR description, citing bff-extensions.md decision criteria (additive facade method on the existing SPE boundary — no new surface).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Graph driveItem versions content endpoint; SPE facade OBO download; ADR-007 boundary discipline</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
