  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>The facade downloads only the item's CURRENT content (`DownloadFileAsUserAsync`, ISpeFileOperations.cs:42) — there is no method to fetch a *specific historical version's* content. No overlap; verified against `ISpeFileOperations.cs`.</existing>
    <extension>This IS an extension of the existing facade — an additive method on `ISpeFileOperations`/`SpeFileStore`, reusing the OBO download pattern. It does not introduce a new service or SPE plumbing; it adds one version-scoped request builder.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without version-content fetch, E1's delta save cannot retrieve the correct load-time baseline after a page refresh (client `state.docxBytes` is gone and the SPE *current* version is degraded by prior dirty saves). Concrete failing contract: FR-06 acceptance "a save after a page refresh still applies the delta onto the correct load-time version" cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `driveId` + `itemId` + `versionId`, the facade method returns that specific version's content bytes (validated against the Graph `/versions/{versionId}/content` route) — per FR-06.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A save after a page refresh (client bytes gone) can still retrieve the correct load-time version by `versionId` (the capability that makes FR-06 acceptance achievable; the end-to-end assertion rides the task 022/024 seam test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a missing/unknown `versionId` returns `null` (facade-translated), not an unhandled `Microsoft.Graph` exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `Microsoft.Graph` type appears in the method's public signature or anywhere above `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure (ADR-007) — verified by inspection / arch test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The method is additive — existing `DownloadFileAsUserAsync` callers and mocks are untouched; BFF build is green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching unit tests exist and pass, mocking at the facade/Graph boundary (no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`) — per NFR-06/ADR-038.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (~0 expected; no new package); PDB convention stated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
