  <notes>
    **Completed 2026-07-16** (Opus 4.8, FULL rigor). Code deliverable done + build green (0 errors).

    **Files modified**:
    - Infrastructure/Graph/ISpeFileOperations.cs — added `DownloadFileVersionAsUserAsync(HttpContext,
      driveId, itemId, versionId, ct) -> Task&lt;Stream?&gt;` (mirrors DownloadFileAsUserAsync; additive).
    - Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs — added the facade delegation to `_driveItemOps`.
    - Infrastructure/Graph/DriveItemOperations.cs — implemented via Graph v5
      `Drives[driveId].Items[itemId].Versions[versionId].Content.GetAsync(...)` under OBO; 404/missing
      version → null (facade error-translation); 403 → UnauthorizedAccessException. Mirrors the
      existing download impl exactly.

    **ADR-007**: verified by inspection — new public signatures expose only HttpContext + string +
    Stream?; no Microsoft.Graph type crosses the facade. Additive: existing DownloadFileAsUserAsync
    callers/mocks untouched.

    **§6.5 Path-C — unit test deferred to the 022/024 seam (AC#6)**: the mirrored method's own unit
    tests (SpeFileStoreTests.cs) are ALL `[Fact(Skip="Graph SDK sealed classes cannot be mocked...")]`
    — Graph v5 GraphServiceClient/request-builders are unmockable at the DriveItemOperations level. The
    only working exercise is FakeGraphClientFactory+FakeGraphHttpHandler THROUGH an endpoint (seam test),
    which needs the consuming endpoint from task 022. ADR-038 bans facade-level scaffolding mocks
    (B1/B5/B7) and mandates seam tests; the POML itself states the through-the-wire test rides 022/024.
    → No scaffolding unit test added. **TRACKING: task 024's E1 seam test MUST assert baseline
    retrieval by versionId (load-time version fetched after a simulated refresh).** SYSTEMIC: this
    defer-to-seam doctrine applies to all R3 BFF facade/IO tasks (010/020/021/022/023) — pending owner
    confirmation.

    **Publish size**: no NuGet/dependency change (Graph SDK already referenced) → compile-only IL delta,
    negligible; absolute unchanged from task 001 (~47.26 MB compressed incl PDBs). Not re-measured (the
    per-task rule targets dependency/size drift; a C#-only method adds none). PDB convention: incl PDBs.

    **Placement Justification (§10)**: additive method on the existing SPE facade boundary — no new
    service/surface; the version-scoped download extends the existing OBO download pattern. In-BFF per
    bff-extensions.md (SPE access is BFF-owned behind SpeFileStore).

    **Quality gate (Step 9.5, inline)**: exact mirror of a shipped method + ADR-007 verified by
    inspection + build green + no new deps. Full /code-review + /adr-check available on request.
  </notes>
